{{!
    @template tool_vae/fiche_results

    The result of an import of records: one item per record, then, when one was imported, the way to say that one replaces
    another.

    Every text comes from the context, worded by tool_vae\output\fiche_results. The template holds no logic. Two keys are
    HTML (triple braces): texthtml, a sentence of the language file that holds what the import said of a record (already
    safe) and the number of the record, escaped by tool_vae\output\fiche_results; nexthtml, a sentence of the language file
    whose link is drawn by the template tool_vae/cell_content.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * items - array of objects {texthtml}: one sentence per record
    * nexthtml - false, or HTML: the way to say that one record replaces another

    Example context (json):
    {
        "items": [{"texthtml": "RNCP99001: imported. 4 competencies added."}],
        "nexthtml": "Does one replace another? <a href=\"https://example.com/supersession.php\">Replacements</a>"
    }
}}
<ul class="tool-vae-fcimport-results">{{#items}}<li>{{{texthtml}}}</li>{{/items}}</ul>
{{#nexthtml}}
<p>{{{nexthtml}}}</p>
{{/nexthtml}}
